<Base title="Updates and corrections" description="A dated record of material changes to Howloop's money guides, calculators and public banking product data, plus how to report an error.">
<header class="hl-page-head hl-wrap"><div class="hl-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Updates & corrections</div><span class="hl-eyebrow">A RECORD YOU CAN CHECK</span><h1>Useful information.<br/>Accountable updates.</h1><p>Material changes to our content and tools belong here. A design edit does not make an old interest-rate snapshot new.</p></header>
<article class="hl-wrap hl-content"><section><h2><time datetime="2026-09-18">18 September 2026</time> — Employee tax return companion</h2><p>Added a <a href="/tax-return">five-step preparation guide</a> with income-year and coverage checks, occupation sources, record reminders, six expense topics, a local expense organiser and downloadable CSV and myTax checklists. Expense arithmetic separates private use and work-use reimbursements; it does not assess tax deductibility. It does not decide deductions, estimate refunds or lodge returns. The guided flow runs without AI; optional AI explanations are disabled until separately configured.</p></section><section><h2><time datetime="2026-09-18">18 September 2026</time> — Australian money tools</h2><ul><li>Introduced compound-interest, mortgage and offset, savings-goal and emergency-fund calculators with assumptions and calculation breakdowns.</li><li>Published the bank explorer with dated public CDR product snapshots. Missing or partial data is labelled. Supported base rates are modelled separately from bonus and introductory components.</li><li>Expanded six money guides with worked comparisons, common mistakes and primary-source references.</li><li>Added a starting-point guide, topic navigation and individual article update records.</li><li>Separated older everyday how-to guides into a labelled archive. Their existing URLs remain available; they are outside the current money-guide library.</li></ul><p><a href="/methodology">Calculation and data methods →</a></p></section><section><h2>How a correction is handled</h2><p>Send the page URL, the part that seems wrong and a source or reproducible example to the address on our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Use sample amounts and leave out account identifiers.</p><p>A verified error in a formula, example or explanation is corrected in the affected page. A material change should be recorded here or in the article's update note. Typographical or layout changes do not need to be presented as a new factual review.</p></section><section><h2>What an update date means</h2><p>A guide's publication date records when it first appeared. Its update date records a material edit; a source-check date records a check of its cited references. Bank retrieval dates describe a separate data snapshot and cannot guarantee a current offer. None of these dates means a licensed adviser has reviewed the page.</p></section><p><a href="/editorial-policy">Read the publishing policy →</a></p></article></Base>

